---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CtaStrip from '../components/CtaStrip.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
import { breadcrumbSchema, localBusinessSchema } from '../lib/schema';

const schema = [
  localBusinessSchema(),
  breadcrumbSchema([
    { name: 'Home', url: SITE.url },
    { name: 'About', url: `${SITE.url}/about` },
  ]),
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About kianlocks"
  description="kianlocks Ltd is a North & Central London locksmith fitting Avocet ABS 3-star high-security cylinders only. Independent, insured, accountable."
  schema={schema}
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'About' }]} />
      <h1>Built for one job. Done well.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        kianlocks Ltd is a London locksmith with a deliberately narrow
        offering: the lock change. Done with one cylinder, fitted by
        one team, to a single uncompromising standard.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <article class="prose">
        <h2>What we do</h2>
        <p>
          We replace the euro-profile cylinder on residential doors
          across North &amp; Central London with the Avocet ABS
          3-star Kitemarked cylinder. {SITE.price} flat —
          {SITE.priceIncludes} included. That is the entire service.
        </p>
        <p>
          We don&rsquo;t do emergency lockouts. We don&rsquo;t cut
          car keys. We don&rsquo;t open safes. We don&rsquo;t fit
          smart locks. We don&rsquo;t carry alternate brands. We do
          one thing, properly, and refer you elsewhere if your job
          isn&rsquo;t that one thing.
        </p>

        <h2>Who we work with</h2>
        <p>
          Three customer types make up almost all our work:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Landlords</strong> changing locks between tenancies — old keys made worthless, insurance-grade cylinder fitted, itemised invoice for the property file.</li>
          <li><strong>Tenants</strong> who&rsquo;ve just moved into a new flat or house and want the previous occupant&rsquo;s keys to no longer open their door.</li>
          <li><strong>Homeowners</strong> upgrading a generic euro cylinder to a 3-star ABS — usually because the door looks vulnerable, the insurer asked, or you&rsquo;ve read about lock-snap attacks.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Why this approach</h2>
        <p>
          The lock-change market in London is broken in a specific way.
          Most callouts arrive unquoted, fit a 1-star cylinder, charge
          for &lsquo;labour by the hour&rsquo;, and leave. Six months
          later the cylinder snaps under attack — because it was always
          going to.
        </p>
        <p>
          The fix is not better marketing. It&rsquo;s a different product,
          a different process, and a different kind of conversation. We
          quote in advance, we fit the only cylinder that meets the
          standard alone, and we tell you exactly what you&rsquo;ve
          received in writing.
        </p>

        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          kianlocks Ltd is registered in England and Wales. Our work is
          covered by full public liability insurance. We have been
          fitting locks across London since 2020.
        </p>

        <h2>What we promise</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>{SITE.price} flat.</strong> No callout fee, no per-minute labour, no upsell ladder.</li>
          <li><strong>One product.</strong> Avocet ABS 3-star Kitemarked cylinder, every job. We do not fit anything else.</li>
          <li><strong>Email-led booking.</strong> Reply within 2 hours during office hours. Quote in writing before you book.</li>
          <li><strong>Written documentation</strong> of every fitting — for your insurer, landlord file, or freeholder.</li>
          <li><strong>Honest scope.</strong> If your job isn&rsquo;t a planned ABS lock change, we&rsquo;ll tell you and recommend someone better suited.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaStrip />
</BaseLayout>
